From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Garcia <lex@ibm.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: add linux ppc64le build target and packaging

Adds PowerPC 64-bit little-endian (ppc64le) as a supported Linux architecture, wiring it through the gulp client/reh/scan build targets, the debian/rpm arch maps and generated dependency lists, the powerpc64le-linux-gnu sysroot toolchain and checksums, the CLI update-service platform detection, and the extension TargetPlatform. Introduced for ppc64le hardware in #1857/#1923 and extended with DEB/RPM/CLI packaging in #2767.

Co-authored-by: Baptiste Augrain <daiyam@zokugun.org>

